# Make a standard orc paladin (lawful good, forced by the class) and stop in
# the dungeon. Included by cannibal-orc-own.keys and cannibal-orc-other.keys
# (tools/check_cannibal_alignment.sh, bd inc-08js). Paladin is chosen because
# only a Good and Lawful eater can show either half of the alignment charge:
# AlignedAct (src/Prayer.cpp) lets AL_NONGOOD move only a Good character and
# AL_NONLAWFUL only a Lawful one.
a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Explore Mode -- continue
@choose "Orc"
@choose "Orc (Standard)"
@choose "Paladin"
a       # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
@until "Choose a feat" a   # Alignment (one entry, Lawful Good) and its help page
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "Unspent Skill Ranks" ENTER
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks
@while "wish to worship" y
@while "personality archetype" a
ESC     # dismiss the arrival room description
